---
import Slide from '@alkemdotdev/alkemist-components/slide';
import Chart from '@alkemdotdev/alkemist-components/chart';
---

<Slide title="A signal loses energy">
  <p>
    Displace an oscillator and release it. The motion continues, but each peak
    is smaller than the last. The curve below is a synthetic analytic
    trajectory: it illustrates damping without claiming an experimental
    measurement.
  </p>
  <p>
    The period describes how often the motion repeats. The envelope describes
    how quickly it fades. Keep those two observations separate.
  </p>
</Slide>
<Slide title="Inspect the trace">
  <Chart
    id="specimen-trace"
    src="/test/oscillation.csv"
    type="line"
    x="time"
    y="position"
    title="Damped oscillator"
    description="Synthetic position over time."
    sample
    parameters={['ink', 'grid', 'zoom']}
  />
</Slide>
